{"registerListener() only checks ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ (V1 feature flag) but not ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2, causing ClientModel.ClientRemovedEvent and GroupModel.GroupRemovedEvent handlers to not be registered when V2 is enabled but V1 is disabled, potentially leaving V2 permissions not updated on client or group removal.": 0.8596091866493225, "Conflicting CONFIGURE scope behavior - V2 redirects canConfigure() to canManage() without a CONFIGURE scope, while another finding says CONFIGURE is defined and should be honored separately. The canConfigure(ClientModel) permits canManage(client) and then checks AdminPermissionsSchema.CONFIGURE, requiring verification against the actual target version.": 0.09723889082670212, "FineGrainedAdminPermissionEvaluator can dereference a null resourceTypeResource during permission evaluation, including paths reached from getIdsByScope/hasPermission when the resource type is unsupported or missing, causing NullPointerExceptions instead of denied or empty results.": 0.32047849893569946}